ce aryans you will put more on byron  left witch's plate let's just say as the  offensive coordinator and so those are  the ways that this rule could help teams  because eventually if bruce arians helps  uh byron leftwich get a head coaching  job bruce aryan says hey we got we got a  couple more third round picks this year  that's going to help us but i i think  it's more of the cumulative effect  as troy vincent talked to me about the  other day and the cumulative effect  meaning  that in conjunction  with the new rooney rule rules this year  which say that every team has to  interview two minority candidates for  head coaching job every team has to  interview at least one minority  candidate for a coordinator job that is  really helped by the nfl to loosen the  log jam  it is an amazing dynamic in the national  football league and it's unavoidable  that you have to  create develop  and enhance the skills of your  apprentices knowing full well  that they may become your arch rivals  before too long and a lot of other  businesses especially smaller businesses  the people in charge they're not going  to show some  some potential future competitor how  it's done right you don't want them  setting up shop across the street from  you even in something as simple as a  bakery we're not showing you what our  secrets are you're going to set up a  bakery across the street in the nfl  that's just that's how it works hey our  best case scenario is to have a staff  full of guys who are going to go  throughout the league and create hell  for us and maybe get us fired eventually  because they're so good and we've helped  get them there and you know that's just  part of the reality of the sport  and this specific aspect of it does  incentivize coaches to ensure that the  minority candidates have the same  opportunities as  the son of the coach as the person who  knows this person who knows that person  who gets their their opportunity that  way i think opening the doors on the  fr